      "path": "src/ui/screens/CardMarks.tsx",
      "content": "Focusing the next cell does not select it when that cell is a button: SessionGrid only calls onChoose for button clicks, whereas inputs select on focus. This can create a keyboard focus loop in the normal two-column case: Tab from Monday's input enters its editor, Tab from the editor focuses Friday's saved-Mark button, and Tab from Friday falls through to the still-mounted Monday editor below the table, whose last control sends focus back to Friday indefinitely. Select the destination observation when advancing to a button cell (or otherwise ensure the old editor is not revisited), and add a regression test that continues tabbing after reaching the next saved-Mark cell, including when it is the last grid cell.",
      "existing_code": "    else if (!event.shiftKey \u0026\u0026 target === controls[controls.length - 1]) go(cells[cells.indexOf(cell as HTMLElement) + 1]);",
      "start_line": 327,
      "end_line": 327,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/CardMarks.tsx",
      "content": "The chosen cell can be absent from the displayed table after changing the earlier-sessions page: paging leaves `chosen` and its editor intact. In that case `cell` is undefined, so `indexOf` returns -1 and Tab from the editor's last control unexpectedly focuses the first grid cell (and can replace the editor), rather than continuing past the editor. Only redirect to a successor when the chosen cell was actually found; otherwise allow normal Tab navigation. Add coverage for tabbing through an editor after paging its cell out of view.",
